Z||000010||LZeitgeist||05-23-2001||03:13 PM||||I think someone jacked up their GT in their driveway, took a pic, and placed it on a dragstrip with Photoshop. <P>I'm not saying it's impossible, but in that particular pic, I just have a feeling it was a retouch rather than a real event. Just some elements of the photo look fishy to me, although if it's a retouch, it's rather well done.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||05-23-2001||04:03 PM||||Well, I don't think you'd get much sidewall wrinkle on street tires.  They'd break traction first.  Which makes it hard to believe a wheelie on street tires.  Also, the rear suspension doesn't look compressed.  If the car's pulling a wheel stand, the rear should squat under the torque and the extra weight beign transferred to the rear wheels.  IF it's a cut/paste, it's pretty awesome since the scenery visible through the windows matches well.  I'm more inclined to believe the jack at the track.||||reg||11
Z||000012||stsmithgt||05-23-2001||04:17 PM||||I noticed the back end wasn't down in the dirt where it should have been.  My brother had a 70 Challenger RT that would pop wheelies without squating much, but we had his air shock pumped up solid.(old school) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  A 440 6-pack helped the front end up.(I miss that car)||||reg||1
